     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;font:normal normal normal 13.2px/normal Monaco\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Why is the second-order- factor &quot;Com&quot; of my first-order &quot;Loy&quot; set to 1?</font></p><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;font:normal normal normal 13.2px/normal Monaco\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I would have expected two values describing &quot;Loy&quot;.</font></p><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;font:normal normal normal 13.2px/normal Monaco\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></p><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;font:normal normal normal 13.2px/normal Monaco\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Thanks Christina</font></p><p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 4.0px;font:13.2px Monaco;color:#b01300\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 4.0px;font:13.2px Monaco;color:#b01300\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 4.0px;font:13.2px Monaco;color:#b01300\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"># Regression </font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 4.0px;font:13.2px Monaco;color:#b01300\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   <span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> Tru ~ Exp + Sat</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 4.0px;font:13.2px Monaco;color:#b01300\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   <span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> Sat ~ Exp</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 4.0px;font:13.2px Monaco;color:#b01300\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   <span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> Loy ~ Exp</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 4.0px;font:13.2px Monaco;color:#b01300\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   <span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> Loy ~ Sat</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 4.0px;font:13.2px Monaco;color:#b01300\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">         Loy ~ Tru </font></p></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div> Loy =~</div><div>    Com     1.000</div><div>    Rec     0.927    0.087   10.703    0.000</div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>It&#39;s hard to tell exactly what you are modeling without seeing the full syntax.  The output shows that Loy is defined by Com and Rec, yet you describe Com as a second-order factor and Loy as a first-order factor, which might imply the opposite (i.e., if Com is a latent construct that is an indicator of Loy, then Loy must be a higher-order factor). <br><br>As far as the factor loading = 1 is concerned, the default setting in sem() is to identify the construct by fixing the first loading to 1, but you can override that in the syntax (e.g., Loy =~ NA*Com) or in the call to sem() by choosing a different method of identification: sem(model, data, <a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792432039035000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1P3vuKS5J0ZO-y2urcRzqU\">std.lv</a> = TRUE).  Again, without seeing your full syntax, it&#39;s hard to see the problem.<br><br>Terry<br><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
